    "details": "<p><strong>Tech Mafia</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a team-based technical social deduction game that combines </span><strong>coding, debugging, AI prompting, logical reasoning, strategy, deception, and teamwork</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Participants will register individually but will be assigned a team at the beginning of Round 1. They shall compete in teams of </span><strong>6</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, but there is a hidden conflict within every team.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the beginning of the event, each participant receives a secret role card. In every team:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>4 participants are Innocents</strong></li>\n<li><strong>2 participants are Mafia&nbsp;</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Innocents must work together to complete technical challenges as efficiently as possible.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Mafia have a completely different objective: </span><strong>slow down, mislead, and sabotage their team without being identified.</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Across the first two rounds, participants must balance two things - </span><strong>performing well and figuring out who they can trust.</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the end of Round 2, every team must identify its suspected Mafia members. The outcome of this decision determines which participants advance to the final round.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Round 3 eliminates the team element completely.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The remaining participants compete individually through a series of technical and mental challenges, with the </span><strong>Top 3 performers becoming the final winners of Tech Mafia.</strong></p>",
